SPEC = {'file': 'cover_lovable_data_scientist_agent', 'label': 'Lovable Data Scientist Agent', 'center': True, 'paras': ['I am writing to apply for the Data Scientist, Agent position at Lovable in London. I am completing an MSc in Health Data Science at University College London, where a distinction is expected, after a BSc in Biological Sciences at Imperial College London, and I currently work as a Data Analyst Intern at TikTok Shop UK. This role is unusually close to what I have actually done: defining what a good AI answer looks like when there is no clean answer key, building the evaluation system that scores it, and testing whether a change actually made the system better.', 'What attracts me most to Lovable is that the data scientist owns agent quality rather than reporting on it. Deciding whether an agent change ships needs metrics that people trust, experiments that work with noisy outcomes, and evaluations that keep running as the agent evolves. I enjoy taking an unclear business problem, identifying what users actually need, and turning it into a workflow that can be tested and improved, and a small, fast team working directly with the engineers is where I work best.', "My LLM evaluation experience is direct. At DS Digital Technology I worked on a medical AI engagement where I built Python pipelines that called six LLM APIs with retrieval and multi-step workflows and automated the processing and scoring of over 2,400 records. There was no answer key, so I designed one with the client's clinical experts: a 246-question benchmark and a six-dimension rubric with red-line rules that the client adopted as its acceptance standard, scored through an LLM-as-judge framework. I also co-built a scientifically reviewed knowledge graph and ran blinded A/B tests to measure whether it actually improved output quality, rather than assuming it did.", 'At TikTok Shop UK I am a Data Analyst Intern, where I analyse merchant and transaction data in SQL and Python and build the KPI frameworks and dashboards that operations, product and commercial teams use to set targets and track initiatives. Alongside my analytical work I built an AI agent that automates repetitive steps of the analytics workflow, which has been adopted by my own team and by partner teams. Building it meant understanding an existing workflow in detail, deciding which steps to automate, and then supporting colleagues as they began to rely on it. I use Claude Code in my development work and review the code it produces rather than accepting it unchecked.', 'On experimentation and statistics, my MSc work is grounded in exactly the questions you describe. My dissertation builds predictive and causal models on 458,840 UK Biobank participants, using doubly robust causal forests and sensitivity analyses to separate real effects from noise, and is delivered as a deployed Streamlit application. I also led a group project building a clinical NLP pipeline with fine-tuned transformer models and an evaluation framework that surfaced where vision-language models failed.', "Thank you for considering my application. I would welcome the opportunity to discuss how my experience with LLM evaluation, experimentation and agent building could help make Lovable's agent measurably better."]}
